      q: "What is TAI time?",
      a: "TAI stands for Temps Atomique International (International Atomic Time). It is a pure atomic timescale that ticks strictly without leap seconds. UTC is currently 37 seconds behind TAI."
    },
    {
      q: "What is UT1 time?",
      a: "UT1 is astronomical time derived from Earth's rotation relative to distant quasars and stars. UTC is kept within 0.9 seconds of UT1 by adding leap seconds."
