        <strong>Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) is the primary atomic time standard by which the world regulates civil clocks, navigation, aviation, and global financial networks.</strong> 
        Unlike regional time zones, UTC does not observe Daylight Saving Time and remains constant year-round. It is anchored to International Atomic Time (TAI) maintained by over 400 ultra-precise caesium atomic clocks worldwide, and adjusted via leap seconds to remain within 0.9 seconds of Earth's astronomical rotation (UT1). 
